<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela bolivar slips to 470.50/471.50/dlr.</title>
<headline>Venezuela bolivar slips to 470.50/471.50/dlr.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Venezuelan bolivar gently softened to close at a Central Bank-set floor of 470.50/471.50 per dollar, traders said.</p>
<p>On Thursday, the unit closed at 470.00/471.00 per dollar.</p>
<p>&quot;Banks were demanding dollars and there was very little offered. All that I saw came from the Central Bank,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>The market was dry today, traders added, who expected to see a similar pattern of trade for the coming week with the bolivar hovering around 470 per dollar.</p>
<p>-- Oscar Galvis, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600</p>
</text>
